/**
 * The pricing experiment's coin flip.
 *
 * Which price ladder a visitor sees is a *deterministic hash of her funnel id*
 * (FSID / `quizPublicId`), not a PostHog feature flag. Deliberate, for the same
 * reason FSID itself is not PostHog's id: ad blockers are common on this
 * traffic, and assignment through an analytics script would turn an analytics
 * outage into half the traffic silently seeing the wrong price. A hash needs no
 * network, no consent, and no script to have loaded — and the server can
 * recompute it from the same id, so the client never gets to name a price.
 *
 * The static quiz page carries a byte-for-byte copy of `fnv1a` below (it cannot
 * import from src/); `pricing-experiment.test.ts` executes that copy against
 * this one so they cannot drift.
 *
 * Analysis runs in SQL: every client event already carries `quiz_public_id`,
 * so any event joins to an arm by recomputing this hash — plus the
 * `pricing_variant` property stamped on events and the purchase.
 *
 * Ending the experiment is deleting the variant ladder and this file's
 * callers; the archived Stripe prices keep billing anyone mid-instalment.
 */

export type PricingVariant =
  | "control"
  | "founding69"
  | "founding49"
  | "trial49"
